://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/commits{/sha}","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/deployments","created_at":"2026-08-05T16:00:07Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T17:31:44Z","pushed_at":"2026-09-23T18:17:10Z","git_url":"git://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:Agent-Field/CodeAF.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF","homepage":"http://agentfield.ai/","size":196153,"stargazers_count":116,"watchers_count":116,"language":"Go","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":14,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":141,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["agent-fleet","agent-harness","agentfield","agentic-coding","ai","ai-coding","cli-agent","coding-agent","coding-agents","coding-assistant","coding-cli","coding-harness","developer-tools","harness","harness-engineering","llm","open-models","open-source-models","software-factory","terminal-agent"],"visibility":"public","forks":14,"open_issues":141,"watchers":116,"default_branch":"dev","permissions":{"admin":true,"maintain":true,"push":true,"triage":true,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/pulls/1362","html_url":"https://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF/pull/1362","diff_url":"https://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF/pull/1362.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF/pull/1362.patch","merged_at":"2026-09-22T02:17:00Z"},"body":"Two entries in `.github/workflows/ci.yml`'s branch lists.\n\n## Why\n\nI was asked to make sure `santos/dev2` was green before merging, went looking\nfor its checks, and found it has none.\n\n- `PR gate` (`ci.yml`) triggers on `pull_request`/`push` for **`dev`** only.\n- `Full check` (`ci-full.yml`) triggers for **`staging`** and **`main`**, plus a\n  09:00 UTC cron that runs against the default branch.\n- So a pull request based on `santos/dev2` is answered by `license/cla` and\n  nothing else, and a push onto that line runs nothing at all.\n\nFour of my own open pull requests show exactly one check each, which is what\nsent me looking.\n\n`santos/dev2` is where feature work merges many times a day. Whether it compiles,\nis formatted, passes vet, holds the laws, carries a change entry, keeps the\nmanual honest, or passes the full suite of every package it touched has been a\nquestion only a person with a cluster could answer. #1361 records what the answer\nwas when somebody finally asked: the one suite that drives the real binary\nagainst a real model is **7 of 18 subtests red** on that line.\n\nThe comment sits beside the existing note about #372, because it is the same\nfailure one level up. #372 was a test filter nobody remembered; this is a branch\nnobody listed.\n\n## What this does not do\n\nIt does not add the tagged tmux e2e suite to any workflow. That suite needs a\nprovider key and costs money per run, so its cadence is a budget decision rather\nthan a line to add, and #1361 asks for it separately.\n\n## Verification\n\n`.github/workflows/ci.yml` parses (`yaml.safe_load`). No test reads this\nworkflow's triggers: `internal/release/workflow_test.go`'s branch assertion is\non `release.yml`'s push list (`dev`, `staging`, `main`, unchanged), and\n`internal/ci/testtooling_test.go` reads this file's light-job **step list**, not\nits `on:` block.\n\nThe change proves itself: if it is right, this pull request gets a `check` run\nit did not have before, and so does every pull request into this line after it.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues/1362/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues/1362/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues/comments/5770278161","html_url":"https://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues/1361#issuecomment-5770278161","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues/1361","id":5770278161,"node_id":"IC_kwDOTu5AHM8AAAABV-91EQ","user":{"login":"santoshkumarradha","id":29346072,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MzQ2MDcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29346072?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha","html_url":"https://github.com/santoshkumarradha","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-22T02:16:50Z","updated_at":"2026-09-22T02:16:50Z","body":"## Correction: all six are the suite, not the product. Two of my suspicions were wrong.\n\nThe triage is done and every one of the six was the suite falling behind a\ndeliberate surface change. **No defect issue needed filing.** PR #1360 repairs\nthem and all six now pass against a real model:\n\n```\n--- PASS: TestTUIE2E (173.93s)\n    --- PASS: TestTUIE2E/home_opens_on_launch_as_seven_panels (4.23s)\n    --- PASS: TestTUIE2E/a_real_conversation_on_the_panels_and_its_search_card (5.87s)\n    --- PASS: TestTUIE2E/answer_from_home_across_two_windows (15.69s)\n    --- PASS: TestTUIE2E/the_projects_panel_is_the_view_by_project (3.21s)\n    --- PASS: TestTUIE2E/a_refused_task_proposal_draws_no_schema_sentence (69.83s)\n    --- PASS: TestTUIE2E/space_in_the_task_room_pages_the_card (75.09s)\n```\n\nWhere I was wrong, since the reasoning matters more than the verdict:\n\n- **I said the `projects` panel drew no rows.** It drew all four. #1046 pinned\n  `projects` and `spend` to the rail — the RIGHT column — and the helper\n  `panelColumn(screen, \"projects\", tuiPlain/2)` cut every line at cell 60 and\n  read sixty blank cells. The panel was plainly on the screen in the capture I\n  was reading.\n- **I said the asking row was not under `needs you`.** It was. #1046 struck the\n  live count off that heading, and the assertion had been matching\n  `needs you · ` to tell the heading from the front of the gate's own\n  `needs your ok …`. It was matching a string home had stopped drawing.\n- **I said failures 5 and 6 shared a cause.** They do not. #6 fails at\n  `tui_e2e_test.go:1943`; #5 fails in a different file\n  (`refusedargs_e2e_test.go:58`) on a synchronisation wait, and its two real\n  assertions were already passing.\n\nSo the lesson lands harder than the one in the issue, not softer: **a panel\ngeometry helper given a hardcoded column fraction is a check that cannot fail\nhonestly.** It reported four missing rows for a panel that was drawn correctly,\nand it would have gone on doing so through any future change. #1360 replaces it\nwith `panelBlock`, which finds a panel by its heading's own position and bounds\nthe read to that panel's own columns, so a row on the panel beside it still\nfails.\n\nOne cause worth naming for the record: **#1046 alone accounts for four of the\nsix.** One wave moved home's foot clause, moved `here` out of the row margin\ninto the description, struck the count off a heading, and pinned two panels to\nthe rail. Each move was deliberate and entered in the changelog; none of them\ncould be seen by the untagged words gate, because every needle still existed\nsomewhere in `internal/tui3`. That is the blind spot this issue's third\nacceptance item asks to close, and it is now the most valuable of the three.\n\nThe other two causes: #938 replaced a 5s sleep in the refused-proposal scenario\nwith a reminder-card wait borrowed from another scenario, so that assertion was\nwrong from the day it landed; and #905 folded every family on the tasks page\nshut, so the `Down` the room scenario pressed had nowhere to go.\n\nAcceptance items 2 and 3 of this issue are still open and still worth doing:\nnothing runs the tagged suite on a schedule, and nothing cheap catches\nadjacency. `TaskOnTheRunEngine` remains red and is being fixed separately.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues/comments/5770278161/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"santoshkumarradha","id":29346072,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MzQ2MDcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29346072?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha","html_url":"https://github.com/santoshkumarradha","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":31570994053,"node_id":"REFE_lADOTu5AHM8AAAABSeDV888AAAAHWccjhQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues/events/31570994053","actor":{"login":"santoshkumarradha","id":29346072,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MzQ2MDcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29346072?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha","